-- Test: closure capturing local variable
-- The arrow return type is spelled `fn(A) -> B` and a lambda is `fn (x: T) -> T { .. }`;
-- `(i64 -> i64)` in return position and a bare `| x -> ..` are not the language's
-- syntax, so this case was recorded as a parse failure of the compiler rather than
-- of the fixture.
fn make_adder : i64 -> fn(i64) -> i64
  | n -> fn (x: i64) -> i64 { x + n }
